    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d141">

                <pb facs="0241" n="135" sameAs="frus:frus1933-39/pg135"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 U.S.S.R./101: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1934-08-17T10:00:00+03:00">August 17, 1934—10
                            a.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received August 17—6:42 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>256. My 239, August 3, 2 p.m. French Chargé d’Affaires privately states that he
                    has been notified by his Government that there is absolutely no foundation to
                    current and persistent reports that France contemplates a large loan to Russia
                    and credits for the purchase of military material. He also insists that there is
                    no project under consideration for the guaranteeing of commercial credits.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bullitt</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
